#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186082932 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083168 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7e0dbf68-2247-5a47-aac8-c16acc5e710c" :knowledge-point/title "Eliminating the Second Variable"}] :question/id #uuid "06136eef-284e-548f-a57b-f400a05f2cb9" :question/math-academy-id "e-13993" :question/problem "Find the solution $(a,b)$ to the following system of equations using the elimination method:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}a+b=3 \\\\ 4a-b=7\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the coefficient of $b$ in the first equation is $1,$ and the coefficient of $b$ in the second equation is $-1.$ \n\nSince these numbers add to zero, we can add the two equations, *eliminate* the variable $b,$ and solve the resulting equation for $a\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a+\\cancel{b} & =3 \\\\ 4a-\\cancel{b} & =7 \\\\ (a+4a) & =(3+7) \\\\ 5a & =10 \\\\ a & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution must have $a=2.$ However, we still need to find $b.$ To do this, we substitute $a=2$ back into one of the equations. Let's choose the first equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a+b & =3 \\\\ (2)+b & =3 \\\\ b & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $a=2, \\,b=1,$ which can be expressed as $(2, 1).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186082933 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083169 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e562941a-078d-555f-aab6-c59d4c79dfba" :knowledge-point/title "Eliminating the First Variable"}] :question/id #uuid "17cb905e-e692-59b8-964d-c7b50482c11e" :question/math-academy-id "e-13994" :question/problem "Find the solution $(a,b)$ to the following system of equations using the elimination method:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}3a-b=2 \\\\ -3a+2b=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the coefficient of $a$ in the first equation is $3,$ and the coefficient of $a$ in the second equation is $-3.$ \n\nSince these numbers add to zero, we can add the two equations, *eliminate* the variable $a,$ and solve the resulting equation for $b\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\cancel{3a}-b & =2 \\\\ -\\cancel{3a}+2b & =-1 \\\\ (-b+2b) & =(2+(-1)) \\\\ b & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution must have $b=1.$ However, we still need to find $a.$ To do this, we substitute $b=1$ back into one of the equations. Let's choose the first equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3a-b & =2 \\\\ 3a-(1) & =2 \\\\ 3a & =3 \\\\ a & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $a=1, \\,b=1,$ which can be expressed as $\\left(1,1\\right).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186082934 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083170 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bc55e7f0-598a-5244-84ef-6dff74f0c420" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Result of a Transformation"}] :question/id #uuid "98645504-986a-5847-8042-32ced1cf4d14" :question/math-academy-id "e-13996" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x+y=3 \\\\ 6x-2y=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe variable $y$ can be eliminated from the system using the following two steps:\n\n1\\. Multiply the first equation by $2$ and obtain\n\n  $$\n  \\begin{aligned}2x+2y & =6.\\end{aligned}\n  $$\n\n2\\. Add the multiplied equation to the second equation to get\n\n  $$\n  \\begin{aligned}⋯\\,\\,?\\,\\,⋯\\,\\,=4.\\end{aligned}\n  $$\n\nWhat's the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "Let's follow the steps provided:\n\n**Step 1**: Multiplying the first equation by ${\\color{blue}{2}}$ yields the following equivalent system:\n\n![](images/66/66212282ac1369c4ed9cd55773a11fd792fde2b58e749149531327ef55fa966e.svg)\n\n**Step 2**: Next, we add these two equations together:\n\n$$\n\\require{cancel}\n\t\\eqalign{\n\t\t2x + \\cancel{2y} & = 6\\[5pt]\n\t\t6x - \\cancel{2y} & = -2\\[5pt]\n\t\t\\hline\n\t  \t(2x + 6x)  &= (6 - 2)\\[5pt]\n\t\t{\\color{red}8x} &= 4\n\t }\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing expression is ${\\color{red}8x}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186082935 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083171 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "20e61a36-c5bf-598a-a07d-833611ffaee6" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a System of Equations"}] :question/id #uuid "0e96914f-2f28-5fef-8a36-9cf2869b1b43" :question/math-academy-id "e-14000" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}3x-2y=9 \\\\ x-3y=-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe variable $x$ can be eliminated from the system using the following two steps:\n\n1\\. Multiply the second equation by $-3$ and obtain\n\n  $$\n  \\begin{aligned}-3x+9y=12.\\end{aligned}\n  $$\n\n2\\. Add the multiplied equation to the first equation to get\n\n  $$\n  \\begin{aligned}⋯\\,\\,?\\,\\,⋯\\,\\,=21.\\end{aligned}\n  $$\n\nFind the missing expression, and hence find the solution $(x,y)$ of the system." :question/worked-solution "Let's follow the steps provided:\n\n**Step 1**: Multiplying the second equation by ${\\color{blue}{-3}}$ yields the following equivalent system:\n\n![](images/b6/b6daa769fdd6307b6dc1f6e40a42c72cc79a8658362cc4adc9d9730f6607b179.svg)\n\n**Step 2**: Next, we add these two equations together, *eliminate* the variable $x,$ and solve the resulting equation for $y{:}$\n\n$$\n\\require{cancel}\n\\eqalign{\n\\cancel{3x} - 2y & = 9\\[5pt]\n-\\cancel{3x} + 9y & = 12\\[5pt]\n\\hline\n(9y - 2y) & = (9 + 12)\\[5pt]\n{\\color{red}7y} & = 21\\[5pt]\ny & = 3\n\t }\n$$\n\nSo, the solution must have $y = 3.$ However, we still need to find $x.$ To do this, we substitute $y = 3$ back into one of the equations. Let's choose the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-3y & =-4 \\\\ x-3(3) & =-4 \\\\ x-9 & =-4 \\\\ x & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $x=5, \\,y = 3,$ which can be expressed as $(5,3).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186496235 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083169 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e562941a-078d-555f-aab6-c59d4c79dfba" :knowledge-point/title "Eliminating the First Variable"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5c334aca-bc6d-5afd-ba64-0abf9f2a0e50" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2,-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495721} {:answer/id #uuid "5f08559b-7bd8-57c4-b8a1-b3d8a59cbedb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2,-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495724} {:answer/id #uuid "a69ab947-742c-58ff-be30-7b2dafd3b831" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1,-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495885} {:answer/id #uuid "c4b53419-f157-5ccf-bc65-88ffaa1ad2c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-2,-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495942} {:answer/id #uuid "de1200cc-ef4c-5d63-8a3e-229a306a208f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1,-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496000}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a69ab947-742c-58ff-be30-7b2dafd3b831" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1,-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495885} :answer-field/id #uuid "2fc28fbf-4593-5f36-9f43-2c9a8075b6f3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496095}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "245bfd0c-95d5-518b-a318-b7794f20aea2" :question/math-academy-id "q-112395" :question/problem "Find the solution $(p,q)$ to the following system of equations using the elimination method:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-4p-5q=1 \\\\ 4p+2q=2\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the coefficient of $p$ in the first equation is $-4,$ and the coefficient of $p$ in the second equation is $4.$ \n\nSince these numbers add to zero, we can add the two equations, *eliminate* the variable $p,$ and solve the resulting equation for $q:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\cancel{4p}-5q & =1 \\\\ \\cancel{4p}+2q & =2 \\\\ (-5q+2q) & =(1+2) \\\\ -3q & =3 \\\\ q & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution must have $q=-1.$ However, we still need to find $p.$ To do this, we substitute $q=-1$ back into one of the equations. Let's choose the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4p+2q & =2 \\\\ 4p+2(-1) & =2 \\\\ 4p-2 & =2 \\\\ 4p & =4 \\\\ p & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $p=1,\\,q=-1,$ which can be expressed as $(1,-1).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186496321 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083168 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7e0dbf68-2247-5a47-aac8-c16acc5e710c" :knowledge-point/title "Eliminating the Second Variable"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "34b27263-1ea3-5149-b5b1-45c4e39af047" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1,2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495634} {:answer/id #uuid "46cfdcdd-8ea2-59f9-b7e7-2537652e78e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2,1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495672} {:answer/id #uuid "52162320-a354-5108-98cf-368f9ba9529a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2,4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495697} {:answer/id #uuid "aae22c4e-5345-5ed5-9768-84cfa023ccb7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(4,2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495891} {:answer/id #uuid "c6838110-0513-569a-9f67-dc6e6ec6ba8b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(4,1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495944}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c6838110-0513-569a-9f67-dc6e6ec6ba8b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(4,1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495944} :answer-field/id #uuid "d0b2d40f-bae8-56bb-ac21-1ba01f520e4f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496184}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e6813cf3-de76-51d8-a604-b9a29aafe849" :question/math-academy-id "q-169979" :question/problem "Find the solution $(u,t)$ to the following system of equations using the elimination method:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-u+2t=-2 \\\\ 3u-2t=10\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the coefficient of $t$ in the first equation is $2,$ and the coefficient of $t$ in the second equation is $-2.$ \n\nSince these numbers add to zero, we can add the two equations, *eliminate* the variable $t,$ and solve the resulting equation for $u:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-u+\\cancel{2t} & =-2 \\\\ 3u-\\cancel{2t} & =10 \\\\ (-u+3u) & =(-2+10) \\\\ 2u & =8 \\\\ u & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution must have $u=4.$ However, we still need to find $t.$ To do this, we substitute $u=4$ back into one of the equations. Let's choose the first equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-u+2t & =-2 \\\\ -(4)+2t & =-2 \\\\ 2t & =2 \\\\ t & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $u=4,\\,t=1,$ which can be expressed as $(4,1).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186496289 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083170 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bc55e7f0-598a-5244-84ef-6dff74f0c420" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Result of a Transformation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "27bc0cdc-353f-532d-9e72-5d4134dc306f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12u" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495596} {:answer/id #uuid "2c4d075d-4278-5b03-9cff-bfc36c7a7b80" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495609} {:answer/id #uuid "4f00d642-dbe6-5588-b748-10cc498e31ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-16v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495692} {:answer/id #uuid "b10688e7-03a0-52fd-a9ec-998185d14655" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-20v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495908} {:answer/id #uuid "e0ce8c51-f4ec-5bf7-b937-8fb69a6201fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12u+7v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496010}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b10688e7-03a0-52fd-a9ec-998185d14655" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-20v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495908} :answer-field/id #uuid "488ad4b5-5ade-5504-a987-7f0586385f2c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496109}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9acd9d22-5f65-53c2-938f-784bc6a38056" :question/math-academy-id "q-169991" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\{\\begin{aligned}4r+9v=3 \\\\ 8r-2v=1\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe variable $r$ can be eliminated from the system using the following two steps:\n\n1\\. Multiply the first equation by $-2$ and obtain\n\n  $$\n  \\begin{aligned}-8r-18v & =-6.\\end{aligned}\n  $$\n\n2\\. Add the multiplied equation to the second equation to get\n\n  $$\n  \\begin{aligned}⋯\\,\\,?\\,\\,⋯\\,\\,=-5.\\end{aligned}\n  $$\n\nWhat's the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "Let's follow the steps provided:\n\n**Step 1**: Multiplying the first equation by $-2$ yields the following equivalent system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}(\\,4r+9v=3\\,)\\,\\times (-2) \\\\ 8r-2v=1\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}-8r-18v=-6 \\\\ 8r-2v=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Next, we add these two equations together:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\cancel{8r}-18v & =-6 \\\\ \\cancel{8r}-2v & =1 \\\\ (-2v-18v) & =(1-6) \\\\ -20v & =-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing expression is $-20v.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186496304 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083171 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "20e61a36-c5bf-598a-a07d-833611ffaee6" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a System of Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "079eb1f2-96c1-5517-b242-f17c3d9c823c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2,2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495530} {:answer/id #uuid "24924a71-f59a-5441-9df6-4a9f4d8eec8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1,-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495591} {:answer/id #uuid "5c1380ae-1e4d-5132-8d7a-5db398955cfe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1,4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495719} {:answer/id #uuid "94ffa6a1-6040-5707-b9de-64e3e3bc1e7c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2,-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495841} {:answer/id #uuid "9d7c0e89-7100-50a1-84a6-916b3651d842" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(0,9)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495862}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5c1380ae-1e4d-5132-8d7a-5db398955cfe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1,4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495719} :answer-field/id #uuid "9cfedfa2-8e52-5f6f-b268-223d86a4f74d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496152}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "bc7c8fe2-c9a4-5377-a2dc-a158b75703dc" :question/math-academy-id "q-170011" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}4u+5p=24 \\\\ 5u+p=9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe variable $p$ can be eliminated from the system using the following two steps:\n\n1\\. Multiply the second equation by $-5$ and obtain\n\n  $$\n  \\begin{aligned}-25u-5p=-45.\\end{aligned}\n  $$\n\n2\\. Add the multiplied equation to the first equation to get\n\n  $$\n  \\begin{aligned}⋯\\,\\,?\\,\\,⋯\\,\\,=-21.\\end{aligned}\n  $$\n\nFind the missing expression, and hence find the solution $(u,p)$ of the system." :question/worked-solution "Let's follow the steps provided:\n\n**Step 1**: Multiplying the second equation by $-5$ yields the following equivalent system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}4u+5p=24 \\\\ (\\,5u+p=9\\,)\\,\\times (-5)\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}4u+5p=24 \\\\ -25u-5p=-45\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Next, we add these two equations together, *eliminate* the variable $p,$ and solve the resulting equation for $u:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4u+\\cancel{5p} & =24 \\\\ -25u-\\cancel{5p} & =-45 \\\\ (4u-25u) & =(24-45) \\\\ -21u & =-21 \\\\ u & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution must have $u=1.$ However, we still need to find $p.$ To do this, we substitute $u=1$ back into one of the equations. Let's choose the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5u+p & =9 \\\\ 5(1)+p & =9 \\\\ 5+p & =9 \\\\ p & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $u=1,\\,p=4,$ which can be expressed as $(1,4).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186496233 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083171 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "20e61a36-c5bf-598a-a07d-833611ffaee6" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a System of Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "157119ad-5b76-548f-a94f-bee7025201f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3,-5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495555} {:answer/id #uuid "46e470ef-ca26-51e5-aee3-653cf87f3e09" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-1,\\frac{5}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495673} {:answer/id #uuid "86ec9541-d0b1-50d6-838f-9aff4b8c683d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1,-5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495802} {:answer/id #uuid "a10f0a61-fc58-5d61-b389-91be03e48828" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-4,1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495868} {:answer/id #uuid "fa2621a8-8093-5de7-9d44-d7db4e9d303f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-\\frac{3}{2},\\frac{5}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496060}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fa2621a8-8093-5de7-9d44-d7db4e9d303f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-\\frac{3}{2},\\frac{5}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496060} :answer-field/id #uuid "07c72b37-51b5-51e6-86af-9356a0461011" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496075}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "19d2dbdd-1890-5f16-8c5e-f4b760789d4e" :question/math-academy-id "q-170022" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}3u+z=-2 \\\\ 3u-5z=-17\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe variable $u$ can be eliminated from the system using the following two steps:\n\n1\\. Multiply the second equation by $-1$ and obtain\n\n  $$\n  \\begin{aligned}-3u+5z=17.\\end{aligned}\n  $$\n\n2\\. Add the multiplied equation to the first equation to get\n\n  $$\n  \\begin{aligned}⋯\\,\\,?\\,\\,⋯\\,\\,=15.\\end{aligned}\n  $$\n\nFind the missing expression, and hence find the solution $(u,z)$ of the system." :question/worked-solution "Let's follow the steps provided:\n\n**Step 1**: Multiplying the second equation by $-1$ yields the following equivalent system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}3u+z=-2 \\\\ (\\,3u-5z=-17\\,)\\,\\times (-1)\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}3u+z=-2 \\\\ -3u+5z=17\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Next, we add these two equations together, *eliminate* the variable $u,$ and solve the resulting equation for $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\cancel{3u}+z & =-2 \\\\ -\\cancel{3u}+5z & =17 \\\\ (z+5z) & =(-2+17) \\\\ 6z & =15 \\\\ z & =\\frac{15}{6} \\\\ z & =\\frac{5}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution must have $z=\\frac{5}{2}.$ However, we still need to find $u.$ To do this, we substitute $z=\\frac{5}{2}$ back into one of the equations. Let's choose the first equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3u+z & =-2 \\\\ 3u+\\frac{5}{2} & =-2 \\\\ 3u & =-\\frac{9}{2} \\\\ u & =-\\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $u=-\\frac{3}{2},\\,z=\\frac{5}{2},$ which can be expressed as $(-\\frac{3}{2},\\frac{5}{2}).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186496322 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083171 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "20e61a36-c5bf-598a-a07d-833611ffaee6" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a System of Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7fafa5af-89fa-552e-9d37-99a0ff0c13c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495784}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7fafa5af-89fa-552e-9d37-99a0ff0c13c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495784} :answer-field/id #uuid "6417f57a-987a-5069-8f89-b6208b47a753" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496127} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c463ec3-ea31-5348-a3fe-88a258fa06cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495565}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1c463ec3-ea31-5348-a3fe-88a258fa06cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495565} :answer-field/id #uuid "6653396e-4315-5460-bcb5-36e17b99353c" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496131} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09239594-58df-5951-8731-fb79d8985941" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495533}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "09239594-58df-5951-8731-fb79d8985941" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495533} :answer-field/id #uuid "d539a197-988a-599f-928a-ee5cd5973d53" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496188}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e6d35c94-0066-57c2-974f-fbc34e655d44" :question/math-academy-id "q-208823" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-2x+y=6 \\\\ 3x+4y=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe variable $y$ can be eliminated from the system using the following two steps:\n\n1\\. Multiply the first equation by $-4$ and obtain\n\n  $$\n  \\begin{aligned}8x-4y=-24.\\end{aligned}\n  $$\n\n2\\. Add the multiplied equation to the second equation to get\n\n$\\,$\n{{field-1}}$=-22.$\n\n$\\,$\nHence, the solution to the system of equations is $($\n{{field-2}}$\\,,$\n{{field-3}}\n$).$" :question/worked-solution "Let's follow the steps provided:\n\n**Step 1**: Multiplying the first equation by $-4$ yields the following equivalent system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}(\\,-2x+y=6\\,)\\,\\times (-4) \\\\ 3x+4y=2\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}8x-4y=-24 \\\\ 3x+4y=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Next, we add these two equations together, *eliminate* the variable $y,$ and solve the resulting equation for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8x-\\cancel{4y} & =-24 \\\\ 3x+\\cancel{4y} & =2 \\\\ (8x+3x) & =(-24+2) \\\\ 11x & =-22\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution must have $x=-2.$ However, we still need to find $y.$ To do this, we substitute $x=-2$ back into one of the equations. Let's choose the first equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2x+y & =6 \\\\ -2(-2)+y & =6 \\\\ 4+y & =6 \\\\ y & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $x=-2,\\,y=2,$ which can be expressed as $(-2,2).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186496237 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083168 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7e0dbf68-2247-5a47-aac8-c16acc5e710c" :knowledge-point/title "Eliminating the Second Variable"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ad0f54d1-cef0-55b5-a40f-2ea684bf7073" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495897}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ad0f54d1-cef0-55b5-a40f-2ea684bf7073" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495897} :answer-field/id #uuid "406c57c3-0b83-51e1-a8dc-6cd72867aba3" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496104} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "830f104c-229f-5076-92bf-3b14a4a50b02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495791}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "830f104c-229f-5076-92bf-3b14a4a50b02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495791} :answer-field/id #uuid "efdc815e-f44f-5378-b5e6-7f7e2759ee7c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496210}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2a39c237-556b-5f05-b0b0-e583ec4b495f" :question/math-academy-id "q-214744" :question/problem "Using the elimination method, eliminate the variable $b$ and find the solution $(a,b)$ to the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}5a-b=19 \\\\ 3a+b=21\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution is $($\n{{field-1}}$\\,,$\n{{field-2}}\n$).$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the coefficient of $b$ in the first equation is $-1,$ and the coefficient of $b$ in the second equation is $1.$ \n\nSince these numbers add to zero, we can add the two equations, *eliminate* the variable $b,$ and solve the resulting equation for $a:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5a-\\cancel{b} & =19 \\\\ 3a+\\cancel{b} & =21 \\\\ (5a+3a) & =(19+21) \\\\ 8a & =40 \\\\ a & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution must have $a=5.$ However, we still need to find $b.$ To do this, we substitute $a=5$ back into one of the equations. Let's choose the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3a+b & =21 \\\\ 3(5)+b & =21 \\\\ 15+b & =21 \\\\ b & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $a=5$ and $b=6,$ which can be expressed as $(\\,5,6\\,).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186496287 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083169 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e562941a-078d-555f-aab6-c59d4c79dfba" :knowledge-point/title "Eliminating the First Variable"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "491bf25a-455b-5640-b303-311ac59d3828" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495676}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "491bf25a-455b-5640-b303-311ac59d3828" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495676} :answer-field/id #uuid "8dd35a45-a54f-5029-8441-374da4f21356" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496146} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "557cb93d-a33e-559e-b0b3-8299452e3ea5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495704}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "557cb93d-a33e-559e-b0b3-8299452e3ea5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495704} :answer-field/id #uuid "da757103-4a78-5e7d-a903-a8f723e1f33a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496195}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "93216753-0c21-5d11-9b15-5ff3cb7c9c57" :question/math-academy-id "q-214761" :question/problem "Using the elimination method, eliminate the variable $a$ and find the solution $(a,b)$ to the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}2a+3b=-5 \\\\ -2a+3b=11\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution is $($\n{{field-1}}$\\,,$\n{{field-2}}\n$).$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the coefficient of $a$ in the first equation is $2,$ and the coefficient of $a$ in the second equation is $-2.$ \n\nSince these numbers add to zero, we can add the two equations, *eliminate* the variable $a,$ and solve the resulting equation for $b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\cancel{2a}+3b & =-5 \\\\ -\\cancel{2a}+3b & =11 \\\\ (3b+3b) & =(-5+11) \\\\ 6b & =6 \\\\ b & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution must have $b=1.$ However, we still need to find $a.$ To do this, we substitute $b=1$ back into one of the equations. Let's choose the first equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2a+3b & =-5 \\\\ 2a+3(1) & =-5 \\\\ 2a & =-8 \\\\ a & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $a=-4,\\,b=1,$ which can be expressed as $(\\,-4,1\\,).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186496330 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083170 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bc55e7f0-598a-5244-84ef-6dff74f0c420" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Result of a Transformation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b8458bcd-0d0b-5300-8add-c0e936140f7b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495921}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b8458bcd-0d0b-5300-8add-c0e936140f7b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495921} :answer-field/id #uuid "af038b03-e90c-5b28-8e5c-49ea18523247" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496161}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f901cd3e-8444-5f6f-a3d7-293cbaf32791" :question/math-academy-id "q-214923" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations. \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x-5y=-12 \\\\ x+3y=20\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe variable $x$ can be eliminated from the system using the following two steps:\n\n1\\. Multiply the first equation by $-1$ and obtain\n\n  $$\n  \\begin{aligned}-x+5y & =12.\\end{aligned}\n  $$\n\n2\\. Add the multiplied equation to the second equation to get\n\n$\\,$\n{{field-1}}\n$=32.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's follow the steps provided:\n\n**Step 1**: Multiplying the first equation by $-1$ yields the following equivalent system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}(\\,x-5y=-12\\,)\\,\\times (-1) \\\\ x+3y=20\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}-x+5y=12 \\\\ x+3y=20\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Next, we add these two equations together:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\cancel{x}+5y & =12 \\\\ \\cancel{x}+3y & =20 \\\\ (5y+3y) & =(12+20) \\\\ 8y & =32\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186496256 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083171 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "20e61a36-c5bf-598a-a07d-833611ffaee6" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a System of Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f4b49429-8318-56b6-8df8-39ba48295a24" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "17x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496042}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f4b49429-8318-56b6-8df8-39ba48295a24" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "17x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496042} :answer-field/id #uuid "8c3a012d-1823-57d7-8ec1-d0018ef54dc1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496144} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3cb9a4bb-1a19-51d9-9cde-466f6655c438" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495649}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3cb9a4bb-1a19-51d9-9cde-466f6655c438" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495649} :answer-field/id #uuid "9e806076-e575-50e7-b5b9-277191f3a351" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496153} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5a4082dc-ea02-571b-91a9-6feb51af2590" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495715}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5a4082dc-ea02-571b-91a9-6feb51af2590" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495715} :answer-field/id #uuid "af99520f-4a2e-5053-ac82-1a56943761ba" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496162}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "556f0a6c-cc10-596c-af86-510be6d1796b" :question/math-academy-id "q-214929" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}3x-2y=22 \\\\ 5x+8y=14\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe variable $y$ can be eliminated from the system using the following two steps:\n\n1\\. Multiply the first equation by $4$ and obtain\n\n  $$\n  \\begin{aligned}12x-8y=88.\\end{aligned}\n  $$\n\n2\\. Add the multiplied equation to the second equation to get\n\n$\\,$\n{{field-1}}$=102.$\n\n$\\,$\nHence, the solution to the system of equations is $($\n{{field-2}}$\\,,$\n{{field-3}}\n$).$" :question/worked-solution "Let's follow the steps provided:\n\n**Step 1**: Multiplying the first equation by $4$ yields the following equivalent system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}(\\,3x-2y=22\\,)\\,\\times (4) \\\\ 5x+8y=14\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}12x-8y=88 \\\\ 5x+8y=14\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Next, we add these two equations together, *eliminate* the variable $y,$ and solve the resulting equation for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}12x-\\cancel{8y} & =88 \\\\ 5x+\\cancel{8y} & =14 \\\\ (12x+5x) & =(88+14) \\\\ 17x & =102\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution must have $x=6.$ However, we still need to find $y.$ To do this, we substitute $x=6$ back into one of the equations. Let's choose the first equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x-2y & =22 \\\\ 3(6)-2y & =22 \\\\ 18-2y & =22 \\\\ -2y & =4 \\\\ y & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $x=6,\\,y=-2,$ which can be expressed as $(\\,6,-2\\,).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186496305 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083171 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "20e61a36-c5bf-598a-a07d-833611ffaee6" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a System of Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1087c4b9-e66f-50c2-af9c-fedd390f7aaf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495550}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1087c4b9-e66f-50c2-af9c-fedd390f7aaf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495550} :answer-field/id #uuid "11f24b84-29c7-5ea3-994a-347c1423e995" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496081} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0fdfbb6f-635b-50a9-a78f-65d2ccca146d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "23x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495549}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0fdfbb6f-635b-50a9-a78f-65d2ccca146d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "23x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495549} :answer-field/id #uuid "61516ff6-1b8b-57bc-beda-125d5fa09d40" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496124} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9d7291ce-0a12-5abe-94a9-1c76e85f8ef3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495861}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9d7291ce-0a12-5abe-94a9-1c76e85f8ef3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495861} :answer-field/id #uuid "f9127678-270e-5d7a-8789-da961ddd1e42" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496216}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "bf584b44-9c54-5ec1-a82b-06a2c468d305" :question/math-academy-id "q-214930" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-5x+7y=-20 \\\\ 4x-y=-7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe variable $y$ can be eliminated from the system using the following two steps:\n\n1\\. Multiply the second equation by $7$ and obtain\n\n  $$\n  \\begin{aligned}28x-7y=-49.\\end{aligned}\n  $$\n\n2\\. Add the multiplied equation to the first equation to get\n\n$\\,$\n{{field-1}}$=-69.$\n\n$\\,$\nHence, the solution to the system of equations is $($\n{{field-2}}$\\,,$\n{{field-3}}\n$).$" :question/worked-solution "Let's follow the steps provided:\n\n**Step 1**: Multiplying the second equation by $7$ yields the following equivalent system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-5x+7y=-20 \\\\ (\\,4x-y=-7\\,)\\,\\times (7)\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}-5x+7y=-20 \\\\ 28x-7y=-49\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Next, we add these two equations together, *eliminate* the variable $y,$ and solve the resulting equation for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-5x+\\cancel{7y} & =-20 \\\\ 28x-\\cancel{7y} & =-49 \\\\ (-5x+28x) & =(-20-49) \\\\ 23x & =-69\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution must have $x=-3.$ However, we still need to find $y.$ To do this, we substitute $x=-3$ back into one of the equations. Let's choose the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x-y & =-7 \\\\ 4(-3)-y & =-7 \\\\ -12-y & =-7 \\\\ -y & =5 \\\\ y & =-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $x=-3,\\,y=-5,$ which can be expressed as $(\\,-3,-5\\,).$"}]}
